    {"topic": "Oxygen Therapy - Targets and Complications", "subtopic": "copd_asthma_treatment", "content": "Oxygen therapy: goal SpO2 88-92% in COPD (avoid high SpO2 = CO2 retention via Haldane effect), 94-98% in asthma. Long-term home O2: improves survival if used ≥15 hours/day (NOTT, MRC trials), especially resting hypoxemia (PaO2 <55 mmHg or SaO2 <88%). Supplemental O2 in exacerbations: titrate to SpO2 target, monitor ABG for hypercapnia. Complications: CO2 retention (reduced hypoxic ventilatory drive in COPD), absorption atelectasis, dry airway secretions (humidify). Mask/nasal cannula tolerance important for adherence.", "tags": ["copd", "asthma", "oxygen"], "library": "intern_year_medicine"},
